 Save bibliographic query responses or an equivalent evidence record in a dated `metadata/` directory. The existing manuscript audits are fixed historical snapshots; a catalog addition does not change them.
 
+When a formal PMLR version adds authors that are absent from the linked DBLP
+preprint record, keep the final ordered author list and set
+`publication_author_source` to the same proceedings URL as `paper_url` and
+`publication_source`. Save a `publication_author_evidence` record containing that
+URL, the verified DBLP identity, title, authors, venue, year, publisher, and the
+PMLR page's `citation_metadata` fields in the
+dated metadata directory. The checker still verifies the DBLP identity and title,
+and requires its original authors to remain in the same relative order. Missing
+evidence, different identities or titles, and unsupported author changes fail;
+use curator review for other changes.
+
